[{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>State each of the following:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>The area of a circle in terms of its radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>The area of an equilateral triangle in terms of its side length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>The volume of a cylinder <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in terms of its radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and its height <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>The volume of a sphere in terms of its radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>The surface area of a sphere in terms of its radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>The volume of a cone with base of radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and height <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=\\pi r^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=\\frac12x^2\\sin60^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt3}4x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=\\pi r^2h\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=\\frac43\\pi r^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=4\\pi r^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=\\frac13\\pi r^2h\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Given</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=\\frac12\\pi r^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dr}{dt}=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dt}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=10x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dx}{dt}=-\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dt}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=2x^3-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dx}{dt}=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dP}{dt}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M=-2x^5+x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dM}{dt}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dr}=\\pi r,\\qquad\\frac{dA}{dt}=\\frac{dA}{dr}\\times\\frac{dr}{dt}=\\pi r\\times2=2\\pi r\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=20x,\\qquad\\frac{dy}{dt}=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\times\\frac{dx}{dt}=20x\\times-0.5=-10x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dP}{dx}=6x^2-1,\\qquad\\frac{dP}{dt}=\\frac{dP}{dx}\\times\\frac{dx}{dt}=3(6x^2-1)=18x^2-3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dM}{dx}=-10x^4+2x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dM}{dt}=\\frac{dM}{dx}\\times\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\tfrac12(-10x^4+2x)=-5x^4+x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>The side of a square <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is increasing at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\ \\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.23/questions/assets/diagrams/223-q3.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find the rate at which the area <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of the square is increasing when the side of the square is exactly 4 cm.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dx}{dt}=10,\\qquad A=x^2,\\qquad\\frac{dA}{dx}=2x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dt}=\\frac{dA}{dx}\\times\\frac{dx}{dt}=2x\\times10=20x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dA}{dt}\\right|_{x=4}=80\\ \\mathrm{cm^2\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>The radius of a circle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is increasing at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\ \\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.23/questions/assets/diagrams/223-q4.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find the rate at which the area <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of the circle is increasing when the radius of the circle is 5 cm giving your answer in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dr}{dt}=3,\\qquad A=\\pi r^2,\\qquad\\frac{dA}{dr}=2\\pi r\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dt}=\\frac{dA}{dr}\\times\\frac{dr}{dt}=2\\pi r\\times3=6\\pi r\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dA}{dt}\\right|_{r=5}=30\\pi\\ \\mathrm{cm^2\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>The radius of a circle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is decreasing at a constant rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.1\\ \\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.23/questions/assets/diagrams/223-q5.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find the rate at which the perimeter of the circle is decreasing, giving your answer in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dr}{dt}=-0.1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Perimeter: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=2\\pi r\\Rightarrow\\frac{dc}{dr}=2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dc}{dt}=\\frac{dc}{dr}\\times\\frac{dr}{dt}=2\\pi\\times-0.1=-0.2\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Rate of decrease: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dc}{dt}=0.2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>The side of an equilateral triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is increasing at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12\\ \\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.23/questions/assets/diagrams/223-q6.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find the rate at which the area of the triangle is increasing when the side of the triangle is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dx}{dt}=12,\\qquad A=\\tfrac12x^2\\sin60^\\circ=\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}4x^2,\\qquad\\frac{dA}{dx}=\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}2x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dt}=\\frac{dA}{dx}\\times\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}2x\\times12=6\\sqrt3x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dA}{dt}\\right|_{x=2\\sqrt3}=6\\sqrt3\\times2\\sqrt3=36\\ \\mathrm{cm^2\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>The surface area of a sphere is increasing at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12\\pi\\ \\mathrm{cm^2\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the rate of change of the radius of the sphere exactly when its diameter is 6 cm.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dt}=12\\pi,\\qquad A=4\\pi r^2,\\qquad\\frac{dA}{dr}=8\\pi r\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dr}{dt}=\\frac{dr}{dA}\\times\\frac{dA}{dt}=\\frac1{8\\pi r}\\times12\\pi=\\frac3{2r}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dr}{dt}\\right|_{r=3}=\\frac36=0.5\\ \\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>A cube is growing so that its volume increases at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\\ \\mathrm{cm^3\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.23/questions/assets/diagrams/223-q8.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The length of each of its sides is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the volume of the cube <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the surface area of the cube <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that the rate of increase of the surface area of the cube may be given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dt}=\\frac{20}x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence, find the rate of increase of the cube's surface area when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has a length of 4 cm.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=x^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=6x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dV}{dt}=5,\\qquad\\frac{dV}{dx}=3x^2,\\qquad\\frac{dA}{dx}=12x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dt}=\\frac{dA}{dx}\\times\\frac{dx}{dV}\\times\\frac{dV}{dt}=12x\\times\\frac1{3x^2}\\times5=\\frac{20}x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dA}{dt}\\right|_{x=4}=\\frac{20}4=5\\ \\mathrm{cm^2\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>A piston can slide inside a combustion cylinder which is closed at one end. The cylinder is filled with gas whose pressure <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in atmospheric units is inversely proportional to the distance of the piston from the closed end, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.23/questions/assets/diagrams/223-q9.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>It is known that the atmospheric pressure is 1.2 when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is 50 cm. At a different point in time, the distance from the closed end is 25 cm and the piston is moving away from the closed end at 5 cm per minute.</p><p>Find the rate at which the pressure is changing at that point in time.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"p=\\frac kx\\text{ gives }1.2=\\frac{k}{50}\\text{ so }k=60\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=\\frac{60}x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"p=60x^{-1},\\qquad\\frac{dp}{dx}=-60x^{-2},\\qquad\\frac{dx}{dt}=5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dp}{dt}=\\frac{dp}{dx}\\times\\frac{dx}{dt}=-60x^{-2}\\times5=-\\frac{300}{x^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dp}{dt}\\right|_{x=25}=-\\frac{300}{25^2}=-0.48\\text{ atmospheric units per second.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>A sphere is growing so that its volume increases at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\ \\mathrm{cm^3\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the rate of increase of the sphere's surface area when its diameter is 50 cm.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=\\tfrac43\\pi r^3,\\qquad A=4\\pi r^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dV}{dt}=4,\\qquad\\frac{dV}{dr}=4\\pi r^2,\\qquad\\frac{dA}{dr}=8\\pi r\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dt}=\\frac{dA}{dr}\\times\\frac{dr}{dV}\\times\\frac{dV}{dt}=8\\pi r\\times\\frac1{4\\pi r^2}\\times4=\\frac8r\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dA}{dt}\\right|_{r=25}=\\frac8{25}=0.32\\ \\mathrm{cm^2\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>A cylindrical tank with radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm has water being poured into it at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\ \\mathrm{cm^3\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.23/questions/assets/diagrams/223-q11.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The height of water after <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find an expression for the rate of increase of the water level in the tank in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Given the tank has diameter 90 cm, find the rate of change of the water level giving your answer to 3 significant figures.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=\\pi r^2h,\\qquad\\frac{dV}{dt}=10,\\qquad\\frac{dV}{dh}=\\pi r^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dt}=\\frac{dh}{dV}\\times\\frac{dV}{dt}=\\frac1{\\pi r^2}\\times10=\\frac{10}{\\pi r^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dh}{dt}\\right|_{r=45}=\\frac{10}{\\pi\\times45^2}=0.00157\\ \\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>A cylindrical tank with radius 10 cm which initially starts full, has water dripping out of a hole in the bottom at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\\ \\mathrm{cm^3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> per minute. The height of water after <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> minutes is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm.</p><p>Find the rate of change of the water level giving your answer to 3 significant figures.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=\\pi r^2h,\\qquad\\frac{dV}{dt}=-5,\\qquad\\frac{dV}{dh}=\\pi r^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dt}=\\frac{dh}{dV}\\times\\frac{dV}{dt}=\\frac1{\\pi r^2}\\times-5=-\\frac5{\\pi r^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dh}{dt}\\right|_{r=10}=-\\frac5{\\pi\\times100}=-0.0159\\text{ cm per minute}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>Water is being poured into an empty cylindrical cone of vertical height 10 cm at a constant rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6\\ \\mathrm{cm^3\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The cylindrical cone has an angle of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the vertical.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.23/questions/assets/diagrams/223-q13.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the volume of the water <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when it is at height <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=\\frac19\\pi h^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dV}{dh}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dt}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when the cone is full.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\tan30^\\circ=\\frac rh\\quad\\therefore r=\\frac h{\\sqrt3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=\\tfrac13\\pi r^2h=\\tfrac13\\pi\\left(\\frac h{\\sqrt3}\\right)^2h=\\tfrac19\\pi h^3\\text{ as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dV}{dh}=\\frac13\\pi h^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dt}=\\frac{dh}{dV}\\times\\frac{dV}{dt}=\\frac3{\\pi h^2}\\times6=\\frac{18}{\\pi h^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dh}{dt}\\right|_{h=10}=0.0573\\ \\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>Sand is being poured onto a table and forms a pile in the shape of a cone. The height of the cone is equal to the diameter of the base.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.23/questions/assets/diagrams/223-q14.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The sand is poured at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\ \\mathrm{cm^3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> per second. Find the rate at which the height of the pile is increasing when the base has a diameter of 4 cm.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dV}{dt}=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=\\frac13\\pi r^2h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> but since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=2r\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=\\tfrac13\\pi\\left(\\frac h2\\right)^2h=\\tfrac\\pi{12}h^3,\\qquad\\frac{dV}{dh}=\\tfrac\\pi4h^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dt}=\\frac{dh}{dV}\\times\\frac{dV}{dt}=\\frac1{\\frac\\pi4h^2}\\times3=\\frac{12}{\\pi h^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dh}{dt}\\right|_{h=4}=\\frac{12}{\\pi\\times4^2}=\\frac3{4\\pi}=0.239\\ \\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>The volume of a cube with sides of length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres is increasing at a constant rate.</p><p>Show that the rate of increase of the sides, is inversely proportional to the area of one side of the cube.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=x^3,\\qquad\\frac{dV}{dt}=k,\\qquad\\frac{dV}{dx}=3x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{dx}{dV}\\times\\frac{dV}{dt}=\\frac1{3x^2}\\times k=\\frac k3\\times\\frac1{x^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore inversely proportional to the area of one side of the cube.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.23-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>The radius of a circle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> changes at a rate which is inversely proportional to the square of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Given that the rate is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.5\\ \\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when the radius is 2 cm, find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dr}{dt}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that the rate at which the area of the circle, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, changes satisfies <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dt}=\\sqrt{\\frac{16\\pi^3}{A}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dr}{dt}=\\frac{k}{r^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac12=\\frac{k}{2^2}\\Rightarrow k=2\\text{ so }\\frac{dr}{dt}=\\frac2{r^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A=\\pi r^2,\\qquad\\frac{dA}{dr}=2\\pi r\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dt}=\\frac{dA}{dr}\\times\\frac{dr}{dt}=2\\pi r\\times\\frac2{r^2}=\\frac{4\\pi}r\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=\\sqrt{\\frac A\\pi}\\quad(r&gt;0)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dA}{dt}=\\frac{4\\pi}{\\sqrt{A/\\pi}}=4\\pi\\times\\sqrt{\\frac\\pi A}=\\sqrt{\\frac{16\\pi^3}A}\\text{ as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]